# adventureGame conventions

## Layout

- **Playable app:** `web/` (React + Vite + TypeScript + Zustand)
- **Game logic:** `web/src/game/` — pure TS port of combat, levels, factories, pools
- **UI:** `web/src/components/` + `web/src/styles/game.css`
- **State:** `web/src/store/gameStore.ts`
- **Assets:** `web/public/assets/` (base path `/adventureGame/` on Pages)
- **Java original:** repo root `src/` — reference only unless the user asks for Java changes

## Patterns

- Prefer factories/pools for creatures, items, weapons, moves (`*Factory.ts`, `*Pools.ts`)
- Keep combat/level logic out of React components when possible
- Reuse CSS variables from `game.css` (`--menu`, `--game`, `--panel`, etc.)
- New room/debris art: wire through existing room/decor helpers, not one-off paths

## Agent workflow

- Planning → `.cursor/skills/feature-planner`
- Implementation → `.cursor/skills/feature-implementer` with an approved plan
- Visual work → `docs/style-reference/STYLE.md`
